<title>ITALY: Italy minister proposes STET golden share.</title>
<headline>Italy minister proposes STET golden share.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Minister of Industry Pier Luigi Bersani is proposing that the government holds a golden shareholding in state-controlled telecoms holding group STET until the company's full privatisation.</p>
<p>STET is to be merged with Telecom Italia and then the merged group privatised before the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;In my opinion it (a golden share) can be a temporary instrument to bridge the phase in which new mechanisms of guarantee are consolidated,&quot; Bersani said in a interview with daily newspaper Corriere della Sera.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
